# L §4.5 (round 12): known in a window holding the cut, "This holds for everything the version or row brings: ...
# its moves lines (the span in force is undecided)"; HOLE-IMPRECISE unless windows chooses. w (known in
# window(2016-01-20, 2016-02-10)) moves v1 to 2016-01.. (L §5.3). As known 2016-02-01: the span in force is undecided, a
# hole (q1); windows earliest takes w as known on 2016-01-20, so v1 governs from 2016-01 and n is 7 (q2); windows latest
# on 2016-02-10, after the cut, so v1 keeps 2016-06.. and n has no value at 2016-03-01 (q3, as L5_3_moves.test).
# (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.3, writer 5's T-39.)
# (Writer 8: windows earliest and latest are gone; windows each splits the line at the day the version becomes
# known, the window's days up to the cut (seen) and after it (unseen), L §4.4 "That holds for every window ...: a
# version's known (§4.5)". The earliest line is the first part, the latest the second.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

input n: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2016-06..
  known 2016-01-01
  n = 7

version w
  cite s
  known window(2016-01-20, 2016-02-10)
  moves v1 to 2016-01..

ask q1: n law 2016-03-01 as known 2016-02-01
ask q2: n law 2016-03-01 as known 2016-02-01 windows each
ask q4: n law 2016-03-01
=== expect
q1: ? ...
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-02-01
q2 [known of w = 2016-01-20 .. 2016-02-01]: 7
  held: n = 7 (v1), read for 2016-03-01
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-02-01
q2 [known of w = 2016-02-02 .. 2016-02-10]: ?"n: no value at 2016-03-01" (n)
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-02-01
q4: 7
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
